# Frontend UI language & copy (RU)

MatchWear shells are for **Russian** users. Apply when editing buyer-web, seller-web, `ui-web`, or any user-facing strings.

## 1. Russian in the UI

- Labels, buttons, titles, errors, empty states, placeholders → **Russian**.
- English only if the word is already universal for users (e.g. **Username**, **Telegram**, **VK**, brand names). Prefer RU otherwise (`Адрес витрины`, not `Slug`).
- API field names (`shop_slug`, `tid_token`) stay English in code; never surface them raw in labels.

```text
Bad:  <label>Slug (латиница)</label>
Good: <label>Адрес витрины</label>
```

## 2. No explanations in the UI

- Do **not** put teaching / architecture / “для проверок…” / JWT / sandbox essays next to controls.
- Short labels + actions only. If something needs a note for developers → **comment in code**, not on screen.
- Errors may be one short sentence; not a tutorial.

```text
Bad:  subtitle="…отдельная seller-сессия (JWT с client=seller)."
Good: omit subtitle or one plain RU line users need
Bad:  <p>Для проверок используем T-Bank sandbox…</p>
Good: // finance uses T-Bank sandbox in local compose
      <label>T-ID</label>
```

## Don't

- Mix EN form chrome with RU body without a settled loanword
- Dump internal terms (`client=seller`, `finance`, `envelope`) into UI
